    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company enters 2026 after a transformative commercial rebuild that drove record quarterly revenue and broadened adoption of its soft-tissue reconstruction portfolio, including hernia repair and IHR/LPR products. European markets, particularly the UK and Netherlands, contributed meaningfully. Momentum now shifts to a more measured phase as newly expanded territories and the ramp-up timeline for recently hired sales representatives temper near-term growth. While product launches like OviTex LTR and customer education investments are expected to fuel adoption, the outlook is tempered by skeptical market commentary questioning the pace of rep productivity.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership executed an aggressive overhaul in 2025, expanding the quota-carrying sales force to its largest ever and promoting a new Chief Medical Officer to strengthen clinical strategy. The 2026 guidance signals confidence in the rebuilt foundation, yet a back-half- weighted ramp tied to rep productivity curves has drawn external scrutiny. Some commentators question whether hiring timelines and recent strategy shifts align with the growth target, introducing a credibility overhang despite management’s record of delivering the commercial transformation and securing a new credit facility.",
